<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean bond market closed on national holiday.</title>
<headline>S.Korean bond market closed on national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean bond market is closed from Thursday for the annual Chusok festival and will reopen on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the market was noticeably quiet as most market participants took off early for the Korean Thanksgiving holiday.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates closed at 12.40 vs Tuesday's 12.42 pct</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs unchanged at 14.60</p>
<p>* Overnight average call rates at 19.0 vs 18.5</p>
<p>-- Yeom Yoon-Jeong, (822) 727 5647</p>
